{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Your turning.</b> Now this is the opposite of the truth." "<b>Shall be reckoned like the potter's clay.</b> The man." "<b>And formed.</b> From the root יצר, he said on account of \"his Maker does not understand,\" and now the lamed is like the lamed of אמרי לי <small>(Genesis 20:1)</small>."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:50.116083156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}